from pathlib import Path
import json,base64,mimetypes,html
r=Path(__file__).parent
names=['study_pair.jpg','PlayfairDisplay.ttf','Manrope.ttf','paper.jpg','fibre.jpg','ink.jpg','plastic.jpg']
a={n:'data:'+(mimetypes.guess_type(n)[0]or'application/octet-stream')+';base64,'+base64.b64encode((r/'assets'/n).read_bytes()).decode() for n in names}
fonts=''.join('@font-face{font-family:'+f+';src:url('+a[n]+');font-weight:100 900;font-display:block}' for f,n in [('Playfair','PlayfairDisplay.ttf'),('Manrope','Manrope.ttf')])
css='''body{background:#111a24;color:#f5f0e7;margin:0;font:14px Manrope}header,footer{max-width:1240px;margin:20px auto;padding:24px}h1{font:900 32px Playfair}p{max-width:900px;line-height:1.7;color:#bdc5cc}nav{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}button{background:#f5f0e7;color:#172330;border:0;padding:12px 15px;font:800 12px Manrope;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#f0cc28}.gallery{max-width:1288px;margin:auto;padding:0 24px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}.state{min-width:0}canvas{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.state p{font-size:13px}.single .gallery{display:block;max-width:620px}.single .state{display:none}.single .state.active{display:block}a{color:#f0cc28}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}@media(max-width:720px){.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr;max-width:480px}}'''
notes=[('01 / Observe','The same study supplies the control and water-exposed fingertip. The printed mechanism begins before narrowing.'),('02 / Inspect','The photograph wipe compares observed surfaces. In the separate schematic, the vessel narrows and the supporting field changes.'),('03 / Resolve','The observed wrinkles are selected. The printed surface folds above the narrower vessel. No scan or measured deformation is implied.')]
body=''.join(f'<section class="state"><canvas width="1080" height="1920" id="frame{i}"></canvas><p><strong>{title}</strong><br>{desc}</p></section>' for i,(title,desc) in enumerate(notes))
notices=''.join('<h3>'+p.name+'</h3><pre>'+html.escape(p.read_text())+'</pre>' for p in (r/'font_notices').glob('*.txt'))
source='''<details><summary>Sources, rights and scientific scope</summary><p>Actual A/B photographic crops: Guy German, Experimental procedure, supplied by Binghamton University through <a href="https://www.eurekalert.org/multimedia/1072667">EurekAlert</a>, with usage statement allowing sharing with credit to Guy German. A is before exposure; B is after 30 minutes in water on Day 0. C, the later repeat immersion, is not used. Changes: source-preserving crop/mask, grayscale/contrast, compositing, comparison boundary and selected annotations. No authorship, endorsement or photographic time-lapse is implied.</p><p>The independent original mechanism schematic represents sympathetic vasoconstriction, a qualitative loss of underlying volume, and surface folding. It is not anatomical geometry, a clinical scan, a measured diameter/volume change or a map of vessels beneath this particular finger. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15095056/">Wilder-Smith 2004 physiology review</a> and <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3885627/">Haseleu et al. 2014</a>. Wet-grip function remains outside this passage and will be qualified in the full story.</p><p>The available comparison source is 700×282; each panel is about 203×282. The hero crop is shown at approximately 1.9× source width in this 1080p art review. It is authentic source texture, not newly resolved detail. Native 4K macro coverage is not approved; source replacement or reduced size must be settled before production.</p><p>Owner materials reused privately. Static only: film grain is frozen; no temporal focus hunt, edge boil, parallax, audio, or camera choreography has been tested. Caption examples are script placeholders, not timed subtitles. Owner art approval is pending.</p></details>'''
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Curio / Water-wrinkled fingers</title><style>'+fonts+css+'</style><header><p>CURIO BUREAU / ONE-PASSAGE ART REVIEW</p><h1>What happens beneath the wrinkle?</h1><p>Three finished states of one developing explanation. Actual research photographs remain separate from the conceptual printed mechanism. This passage is ready for visual review; it is not animated or approved.</p><nav>'+''.join(f'<button data-state="{i}" aria-pressed="false">{s}</button>' for i,s in [(-1,'All states'),(0,'Observe'),(1,'Inspect'),(2,'Resolve')])+'<button id="heading">Hide heading</button><button id="captions">Hide caption examples</button><button id="guide">Caption guide</button></nav></header><main class="gallery">'+body+'</main><footer>'+source+'<details><summary>Font notices</summary>'+notices+'</details></footer><script>const ASSETS='+json.dumps(a)+';'+(r/'scene.js').read_text()+'</script></html>'
(r/'delivered/Wrinkles_Three_State_Review.html').write_text(page);print('Built',len(page))
